 * Initialize arrays A, B, x and scalars alpha, beta.
 * This mirrors the PolyBench init_array() function, but uses Halide
 * Funcs to fill the Buffers.
 *
 * C version:
 *   x[i]      = (i % n) / n;
 *   A[i][j]   = ( (i*j+1) % n ) / n;
 *   B[i][j]   = ( (i*j+2) % n ) / n;
